# MaCSad board envelope policy

This import-free leaf accepts only the bounded, versioned board envelope for
one server-owned workspace. It returns `ok` followed by raw rows, or only
`error`; the separate row decoder validates every canonical field before use.

## To boardEnvelopeFailure () -> Seq of Text:
    Let result be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "error" to result.
    Return result.

## To boardEnvelopeAccepted (decoded: Seq of Text) -> Bool:
    If length of decoded is less than 1:
        Return false.
    Let tag be item 1 of decoded.
    Return tag is equal to "ok".

## To boardEnvelopeBoundsAccepted (byteCount: Int, rowCount: Int) -> Bool:
    If byteCount is less than 0:
        Return false.
    If rowCount is less than 0:
        Return false.
    If byteCount is greater than 1048576:
        Return false.
    If rowCount is greater than 200:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## To boardCaseIdSeen (caseId: Text, seen: Seq of Text) -> Bool:
    Repeat for value in seen:
        If value is equal to caseId:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## To decodeBoardEnvelope (body: Text, expectedWorkspace: Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let byteCount be length of text_bytes(body).
    If byteCount is equal to 0:
        Return boardEnvelopeFailure().
    If length of text_bytes(expectedWorkspace) is equal to 36:
        Let wireLines be lines(body).
        Let lineCount be length of wireLines.
        Let rowCount be lineCount - 1.
        If boardEnvelopeBoundsAccepted(byteCount, rowCount):
            Let headerFields be split(item 1 of wireLines, "|").
            If length of headerFields is equal to 3:
                If item 1 of headerFields is equal to "macsad-board/1":
                    If item 2 of headerFields is equal to "1":
                        If item 3 of headerFields is equal to expectedWorkspace:
                            Let decoded be a new Seq of Text.
                            Let seenCaseIds be a new Seq of Text.
                            Push "ok" to decoded.
                            Let mutable lineNumber be 2.
                            While lineNumber is at most lineCount:
                                Let row be item lineNumber of wireLines.
                                Let fields be split(row, "|").
                                If length of fields is equal to 10:
                                    Let caseId be item 2 of fields.
                                    If length of text_bytes(caseId) is equal to 36:
                                        If boardCaseIdSeen(caseId, seenCaseIds):
                                            Return boardEnvelopeFailure().
                                        Push caseId to seenCaseIds.
                                        Push row to decoded.
                                        Set lineNumber to lineNumber + 1.
                                    Otherwise:
                                        Return boardEnvelopeFailure().
                                Otherwise:
                                    Return boardEnvelopeFailure().
                            Return decoded.
    Return boardEnvelopeFailure().

## To boardEnvelopeMutationAvailable (routeKnown: Bool) -> Bool:
    Return false.

## To boardWorkspaceOverrideAvailable (requestWorkspacePresent: Bool) -> Bool:
    Return false.

## Test: Board envelope decodes bounded rows
    Let workspace be "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111".
    Let header be "macsad-board/1|1|{workspace}".
    Let row be "case|22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222|mathematics|open|normal|50|-|-|-|43617365".
    Let decoded be decodeBoardEnvelope(header combined with "\n" combined with row, workspace).
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(decoded) is equal to true.
    Expect that length of decoded is 2.
    Expect that item 2 of decoded is equal to row.
    Let emptyBoard be decodeBoardEnvelope(header, workspace).
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(emptyBoard) is equal to true.
    Expect that length of emptyBoard is 1.

## Test: Board envelope fixes workspace and schema
    Let expected be "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111".
    Let other be "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa".
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(decodeBoardEnvelope("macsad-board/1|1|{other}", expected)) is equal to false.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(decodeBoardEnvelope("macsad-board/1|2|{expected}", expected)) is equal to false.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(decodeBoardEnvelope("macsad-board/1|1|{expected}", other)) is equal to false.
    For all booleans requestWorkspacePresent:
        Expect that boardWorkspaceOverrideAvailable(requestWorkspacePresent) is equal to false.

## Test: Board envelope rejects duplicates and cap breaches
    Let workspace be "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111".
    Let header be "macsad-board/1|1|{workspace}".
    Let row be "case|22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222|mathematics|open|normal|50|-|-|-|43617365".
    Let duplicate be header combined with "\n" combined with row combined with "\n" combined with row.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeAccepted(decodeBoardEnvelope(duplicate, workspace)) is equal to false.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeBoundsAccepted(1048576, 200) is equal to true.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeBoundsAccepted(1048577, 200) is equal to false.
    Expect that boardEnvelopeBoundsAccepted(1048576, 201) is equal to false.

## Test: Board envelope exposes no mutation
    For all booleans routeKnown:
        Expect that boardEnvelopeMutationAvailable(routeKnown) is equal to false.
